# Reusable components

- One component per file. The file name matches the named export: `Button.tsx` exports `Button`.
- Named exports for components. Default exports only for `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, and `not-found.tsx`.
- Declare an explicit props type beside the component. DOM wrappers extend `ComponentProps` and accept `className`.
- `components/ui` has no fetching, feature copy, or business rules. Variants and sizes are props, not copied class strings.
- Extract a custom hook when logic is reused, or when a component mixes rendering with non-trivial state.
- If the same structure appears twice, extract a component before a third copy.
- Accessible by default: semantic elements, associated labels, keyboard support, and a visible focus style.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — the same button markup copied at every call site
<button className="h-10 rounded-full bg-foreground px-4 text-background">
  Save
</button>

// ✅ GOOD — one primitive; the variant is a prop
import type { ComponentProps } from "react";

const variants = {
  primary: "h-10 rounded-full bg-foreground px-4 text-background",
  ghost: "h-10 rounded-full px-4",
} as const;

type ButtonProps = ComponentProps<"button"> & {
  variant?: keyof typeof variants;
};

export function Button({
  variant = "primary",
  className,
  ...props
}: ButtonProps) {
  return (
    <button className={`${variants[variant]} ${className ?? ""}`} {...props} />
  );
}
```
